From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: LPC ports (wineserver port objects)

NtCreatePort, NtConnectPort, NtSecureConnectPort, NtListenPort, NtAcceptConnectPort,
NtCompleteConnectPort, NtRequestPort, NtRequestWaitReplyPort, NtReplyPort, NtReplyWaitReceivePort(Ex),
NtRegisterThreadTerminatePort and NtCreateWaitablePort were stubs. Ports are wineserver objects:
named connection ports, client and server communication ports; everything for the server side is
queued on the connection port, a request is kept until replied to and the reply goes to the thread
that waits for it. LPC_CLIENT_DIED and LPC_PORT_CLOSED are delivered. Messages use the 64-bit layout
for 32-bit callers too (as Wine's port test shows Windows' WoW64 does). Shared sections are not
supported (STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED); data is limited to the 304-byte message buffer.
---
